WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:12.171
Idea. A ball hits a flat wall at a right angle. On a curve, the line that touches it at a point is the tangent. The line at ninety degrees to it, through the same point, is the normal.

00:00:12.760 --> 00:00:24.301
Perpendicular lines have gradients that multiply to minus one. So the normal gradient is the negative reciprocal of the tangent gradient: flip it and change the sign.

00:00:24.880 --> 00:00:38.809
Then use y minus y one equals m times x minus x one with the normal gradient. Integer form, a x plus b y plus c equals nought, means clear the fractions by multiplying through.

00:00:39.360 --> 00:00:47.295
These questions ask for the equation of a normal, often in integer form. It all starts from the curve's gradient at the point.

00:00:48.400 --> 00:00:59.041
Method. Step one: find the point on the curve. Step two: differentiate and put in x to get the tangent gradient m. The normal is built from this number.

00:00:59.600 --> 00:01:06.551
Step three: take the negative reciprocal. The trap is using m itself, or forgetting the minus sign.

00:01:07.120 --> 00:01:18.531
Step four: write y minus y one equals the normal gradient times x minus x one. Then rearrange to the form asked, clearing fractions for integers.

00:01:19.640 --> 00:01:35.297
Worked example. A real question from June twenty twenty one. Find an equation of the normal to the curve y equals x cubed minus two x, all times e to the one minus x, at the point one, minus one. Five marks.

00:01:35.880 --> 00:01:45.525
Step one: check the point. At x equals one, x cubed minus two x is minus one, and e to the nought is one. So y is minus one.

00:01:46.080 --> 00:01:58.942
Step two: product rule. u is x cubed minus two x, with derivative three x squared minus two. v is e to the one minus x, with derivative minus e to the one minus x.

00:01:59.520 --> 00:02:09.684
Put in x equals one. The first part is one times one. The second part is minus, minus one, times one. So the tangent gradient is two.

00:02:10.240 --> 00:02:20.970
Now the normal. Take the negative reciprocal of two, which is minus a half. A tempting wrong route is to use two as it is. That is the tangent, not the normal.

00:02:21.520 --> 00:02:28.197
Write the line through one, minus one. y plus one equals minus a half times x minus one.

00:02:28.760 --> 00:02:41.985
Multiply by two. Two y plus two equals minus x plus one. So x plus two y plus one equals nought. This explanation is by olevels dot com, not an official mark scheme.

00:02:43.120 --> 00:02:53.583
Common mistake. A common mistake is using the tangent gradient for the normal, or the reciprocal without the minus sign. Neither line is perpendicular.

00:02:54.720 --> 00:03:12.405
Your turn. Now you try, from June twenty nineteen. f of x is e to the three x times root one plus two x. Part a gives the derivative. In part b, find the normal at x equals nought, in integer form. Write your answer, then choose Continue to Answer.

00:03:13.520 --> 00:03:25.652
Answer. At x equals nought, f is e to the nought times root one, which is one. So the point is nought, one. The derivative is two times one times two, over one, which is four.

00:03:26.240 --> 00:03:41.299
The normal gradient is minus one quarter. The line is y minus one equals minus a quarter times x. Multiply by four: four y minus four equals minus x. So x plus four y minus four equals nought.

00:03:41.880 --> 00:03:50.249
The most common wrong answer uses the tangent gradient, four, as it is. That is the tangent, so the normal marks are lost.

00:03:50.800 --> 00:03:56.661
Remember: point, tangent gradient, negative reciprocal, then the line in the form asked.
